  "operative_text": "Section 1 (new N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-14) subsection 1: Except as otherwise provided in section 62.1-02-03, a mandatory waiting period of three days between the purchase and delivery of a firearm must be imposed on any firearm purchased from a firearm dealer licensed under the Gun Control Act of 1968 [27 CFR 478.41; 18 U.S.C. 923].\nSection 1 (new N.D.C.C. 62.1-02-14) subsection 4: An individual who violates this section is guilty of a class C felony.\nSection 2 (new section to N.D.C.C. ch. 62.1-05) subsection 2: A person may not import into the state, transfer, distribute, sell, possess, or give to another person a bump stock.\nSection 2 (new section to N.D.C.C. ch. 62.1-05) subsection 3: A person who violates this section is guilty of a class C felony. Upon arrest of that person, law enforcement shall seize the bump stock. Upon a conviction under this section, law enforcement shall destroy the bump stock.\nSection 3: During the 2019-20 interim, the legislative management shall study the impact of raising the minimum age to purchase or possess a firearm from eighteen to twenty-one."
}